    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1237">

                <pb facs="0991" n="875" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg875"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/154.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Vice Consul Bevan</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 25, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>State to appropriate authority that companies should not be expected to agree to
                    conform with prospective laws and regulations concerning provisions of which
                    they are not informed, and that the United States Government protests against
                    application of such requirement to American companies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
